{"candidates":[{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/session.repository.ts","symbol":"SessionRelationalRepository.deleteByUserIdWithExclude","start_line":99,"end_line":109,"explanation":"The exclusion filter is `id: Not(Number(conditions.userId))`. It compares the session id against the user id, when it should compare it against the id of the session to keep (`excludeId`). The soft-delete therefore removes every session of the user, including the current one. It spares only a session whose numeric id happens to equal the user id, and that is an unrelated session. This matches the report: the refresh call from the current device gets 401, and an unrelated older session sometimes survives."},{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/document/repositories/session.repository.ts","symbol":"SessionDocumentRepository.deleteByUserIdWithExclude","start_line":82,"end_line":93,"explanation":"The snippet is truncated, so I could not see the filter. The Mongo variant has to use `_id: { $not: { $eq: excludeId } }`. If it uses the user id or the wrong field here, the current session would be deleted in the same way."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.update","start_line":426,"end_line":521,"explanation":"The snippet is truncated, so I could not see the `deleteByUserIdWithExclude` call after the password change. If it passes `excludeId` as the user id instead of `userJwtPayload.sessionId`, the current session is not excluded."}],"fix":{"file":"src/session/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/session.repository.ts","description":"Change the exclusion to the session id, not the user id. Use `user: { id: Number(conditions.userId) }, id: Not(Number(conditions.excludeId))`. Also check that AuthService.update passes `excludeId: userJwtPayload.sessionId`.","replacement_code":"await this.sessionRepository.softDelete({
  user: { id: Number(conditions.userId) },
  id: Not(Number(conditions.excludeId)),
});"}}

fix.replacement_code:
await this.sessionRepository.softDelete({
  user: { id: Number(conditions.userId) },
  id: Not(Number(conditions.excludeId)),
});

